                                                   *                                                                    *
                                                   *                                                                    *
                                                   *      INSTRUCTION EXECUTE SUBROUTINE                                *J
                                                   *                                                                    *
                                                   *                                                                    *
                                                   **********************************************************************
                                                   * FUNCTION   LVDC PROGRAMMING STANDARDS REQUIRE THAT THE INSTRUCTIONS
                                                   *            FOR A GIVEN ROUTINE AND THE ACCOMPANYING DATA WORDS BE
                                                   *            STORED IN DIFFERENT SECTORS. IT IS, THEREFORE, IMPOSSIBLE
                                                   *            TO EXECUTE PROGRAM-BUILT AND MODIFIED INSTRUCTIONS WITH-
                                                   *            OUT FIRST CHANGING THE CURRENT DATA SECTOR TO THE CURRENT
                                                   *            INSTRUCTION SECTOR. THE INSTRUCTION EXECUTE SUBROUTINE
                                                   *            PROVIDES A QUICK AND EFFICIENT MEANS TO EXECUTE THESE
                                                   *            PROGRAM-BUILT INSTRUCTIONS.
                                                   * ENTRY      IEDA     CALL WITH FIRST INSTRUCTION IN SYLLABLE 1,
                                                   *                     SECOND INSTRUCTION IN SYLLABLE 0, AND DATA TO
                                                   *                     BE OPERATED ON IN PQ.
                                                          ORGSS   0,3,0,000,0,3,0
                                                   L.IEDA TABLE   6
W                                                         ORG     L.IEDA
                                                          ORG     *,*,*+(1),*,*,*,*
                                                 +        ORG     *,*,*+1,*,*,*,*
     0 03 1 040  0 03    377  1  13                IEDA   STO     777          SAVE RETURN HOP CONSTANT                  B
     0 03 1 041  0 03    043  0  13                       STO     CW           STORE INST                                B
     0 03 1 042  0 03    375  1  17                       CLA     775          OBTAIN DATA WORD TO BE OPERATED ON, IF ANYB
     0 03 1 043  0 03    000  0  00                CW     HOP     0            EXECUTE PROGRAM BUILT INSTRUCTIONS        B
     0 03 1 044  0 03    043  0  10                       TRA     IEDA1
                                                          ORG     L.IEDA
